\f1\fs22 It was an average building in a district of either managers on their way up the ladder or executives on their way down. The major shareholder of a shell company (that owned a holding company that had, as it turned out, never partnered with anyone currently in the country\'97or even alive, for the sake of proper arm\'92s length property development) was, after the Stickett Inn bombing, a businessman in free-fall with no hope of recovery and not a parachute in sight.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

