\f1\fs22 \'93Mr Siddig?\'94 Gerry extended a hand. \'93Gerry Hardman, Commissioner of Traffic Movement and Property Security. Thank you for seeing me. I know you must be extremely busy.\'94\
Ahmed Siddig ignored the hand. \'93What do you want, Mr Hard Man? Shouldn\'92t you be out finding who bombed my property?\'94\
Gerry winced at the way Siddig split the syllables of his name. He pressed on. \'93Terrible business, this. A respected Airborne like you doesn\'92t deserve such misfortune. There should be a law against it.\'94\
\'93That\'92s right. The taxing insurance company refuses to pay. I was forced by the city to demolish. Looks like some holier Airborne already has their eye on buying me out\'97at Cloudborne prices. Right now, I own the most expensive hole in Ulyssia.\'94\
\'93I may be able to assist you, Mr Siddig.\'94\
\'93Oh? TRAMPS is in the market for a hole in the ground, is it?\'94\
Gerry gave his best travelling-salesman smile. \'93Traffic Movement and Property Security is, in fact, looking to lease a hole in the ground.\'94\
\'93What for?\'94\
\'93That\'92s a matter of national security.\'94\
Siddig\'92s eyes lit up with sudden hope. \'93National security costs extra.\'94\
\'93It always does, Mr Siddig. But if you\'92re willing to sharpen your pencil, I\'92m sure I could persuade your insurer to\'85 let\'92s say, appreciate your service to the great Meritocracy of Ulyssia in this time of need.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl220\sb220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 <!$Scr_Ps::1><$Scr_Ps::0>
\f1\fs22 As arranged, and to provide cover for the secret handover, Siddig agreed to lease all plant and equipment on site. The deal done, he left on a \'93business trip\'94 to create distance and plausible deniability. Gerry\'92s team made sure every extra machine carried the same brands and logos as Siddig\'92s gear, and every worker wore the same overalls as before. To any casual observer, it was the same crew of regular Joes. No one could have guessed how many were actually TRAMPS or PAPER agents in disguise.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

