\f1\fs22 But one observer was far from casual. He\'92d been hoovering up every intel scrap about the bombing, and the demolition, and the Stickett Inn\'92s new afterlife as a pop-up. He ran facial recognition on every drone shot of drinkers and work crews, and his stomach dropped the moment police turned up disguised as labourers. His paranoia only increased as truck convoys lined the blocks, carting away tonnes of spoil\'97evidence of serious tunnelling. He tightened the knot of his black tie. When he spotted a load of explosives being carried in under tarps, Agent Jones knew, without a doubt, who was orchestrating this clandestine dig.\
Jihad Man.
